{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310642,"nonce":"zL3UBXnY0y701RFfH1n6LRTrVh4=","title":"LLVM JIT panicked on Not applied to a pointer (any null-check short-circuit); behind it, an abstract's @:to Int-\u003eFloat lowers as bitcast ...","message":"Found via `benchmark_runner orchestration_overhead --single-target rayzor-llvm`,\nwhich reported only `child exited 101`. **The runner swallows the child's\nstderr — use `--single-target \u003cname\u003e` (a hidden flag) to see the real panic.**\n\n**FIXED — Not on a pointer.** `llvm_jit_backend.rs` `compile_unop` called\n`.into_int_value()` unconditionally, and inkwell panics with\n\"Found PointerValue ... but expected the IntValue variant\". Reached by\n\n```haxe\nif (envIters != null \u0026\u0026 envIters.length \u003e 0)\n```\n\n— a String null test whose `\u0026\u0026` short-circuit lowers through `Not` on the\npointer. Broadly reachable, not exotic. Now `ptrtoint`s the operand, which for\na Bool result is exactly the null test the source asked for. `Neg` on a pointer\nreturns a legible Err instead of an inkwell unwrap panic.\nOracle: `compiler/tests/haxe/test_null_check_shortcircuit.hx`.\n\n**STILL OPEN, uncovered behind it:**\n```\nInvalid bitcast\n  %4 = bitcast ptr %1 to double\nLLVM verification failed for function 'toFloat' (IrFunctionId(150069))\n```\n`haxe/Int32.hx:248` is `@:to private inline function toFloat():Float return this;`\nTwo things are wrong at once:\n1. the abstract's `this` arrives as a POINTER where it should be a scalar Int\n   (the boxing family — see [[bugs_generic_scalar_field_stores_box_pointer]]);\n2. an Int-\u003eFloat conversion is lowered as `bitcast`, which is wrong regardless\n   of operand kind — it must be `sitofp`.\n\nFixing (2) alone would turn an LLVM verifier abort into a silently wrong number\nif (1) still delivers a pointer, so diagnose (1) FIRST. `UInt.hx:309` has the\nsame `@:to toFloat` shape and is presumably equally affected.\n\nThis blocks `rayzor-llvm` on the orchestration_overhead benchmark, which is\ncharted on the published site with only two rayzor targets as a result.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_published_bench_lost_and_faked_rows]],\n[[bugs_std_string_dynamic_unbox_and_erased_generics]].\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): FIXED: `s != null \u0026\u0026 ...` PANICKED the LLVM JIT (Not on a pointer). OPEN behind it: `@:to toFloat` emits `bitcast ptr to double`. Runner hides panics — use `--single-target`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_llvm_unop_and_abstract_to_bitcast` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}